# Environment configuration

Copy this file to `.env` for local development when you want to override defaults. Do not commit secrets or production credentials.

```env
# MySQL database
# Set the real password only in your local .env or hosting provider secrets.
MYSQL_HOST=127.0.0.1
MYSQL_PORT=3306
MYSQL_DATABASE=secure_vision
MYSQL_USER=secure_vision_app
MYSQL_PASSWORD=

# Upload limits
MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=5000000
MAX_VIDEO_UPLOAD_BYTES=50000000
MAX_VIDEO_SECONDS=120
VIDEO_SAMPLE_FPS=1

# Recognition
EMBEDDING_MODEL_NAME=Facenet512
EMBEDDING_DISTANCE_THRESHOLD=0.375

# Image quality
QUALITY_BLUR_THRESHOLD=40
MIN_BRIGHTNESS=35
MAX_BRIGHTNESS=225

# Liveness / anti-spoofing
# Keep false until DeepFace anti-spoofing has been validated locally.
LIVENESS_ENABLED=false
```

For Render or another hosting provider, configure these values as service environment variables rather than committing a `.env` file.

When liveness is validated, set `LIVENESS_ENABLED=true` in the local/hosting environment and restart the service. The application fails closed when the anti-spoofing result is unavailable while liveness is enabled.